WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.480
What is the test? What is the idea?

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.220
The test is to show that you people are ridiculous.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.840
I’m giving Roberto Refinetti a hard time here because

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.180
he is the editor of the journal “Sexuality and Culture.”

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.080
He agreed to talk to me after his journal

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.620
was hoaxed by these people.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.920
*Laughter* Dog Park

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.980
They submitted absurd papers

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.920
to twenty academic journals.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.340
One paper included gibberish about rape culture

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.840
in dog parks.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.100
Another was a section of Mein Kampf re-written with

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.960
feminist buzzwords.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.960
Editors of 7 journals published them,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.120
proving, say the hoaxers, that:

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.340
Making absurd and horrible ideas sufficiently political

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.480
fashionable can get them validated at the highest levels

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.100
of academic grievance studies.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.940
Six of the journal editors wouldn't talk to me,

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.340
but Refinetti did.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.136
Let’s look into things and see if we should continue

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.240
doing what we’re doing.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.400
Maybe you shouldn't be doing what you're doing

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:02.040
because it's gibberish, and they've proved it.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.580
Yeah. They didn’t prove, that's the problem.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.700
They sent the articles to 20 different journals

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.980
without asking them if you could study them,

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.440
which is a basic requirement in research these days.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.540
But if they’d asked the journals

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.800
They couldn't have done the test.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.260
But you’re deceiving people without much of a reason.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.520
I think the hoaxers had good reason.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.400
Their hoax woke us up to the fact that

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.160
some academic journals publish nonsense.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.020
The paper Refinetti’s journal accepted titled,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.120
“Going in through the back door”,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.820
claimed you could reduce

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.760
Straight male homo hysteria and transphobia

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.600
through receptive, penetrative sex toy use.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.820
Correct.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:46.360
Sounds like, "Oh, it's not your everyday article."

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.380
And it's not.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.320
This is a specialized journal that deals with

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.620
sexuality and culture.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.100
Will decrease transphobia and increase feminist values.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:55.980
Mm hmm.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.440
Yeah. What is the problem with that?

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.500
I don't see a problem.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.500
Again, it's a statement that could be correct.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.740
It's nothing really absurd or unusual.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.299
But then why publish it?

00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:14.200
Oh, okay. Yeah, that's an issue in publication.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.120
That's the specialization. We've been doing that

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.460
for maybe 100 years.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.680
Seems silly.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.500
Yeah. Okay. So what is silly?

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.480
Ahmm.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.980
Is the respiration mechanism in an ant

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.180
not silly?

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.560
The way an ant breathes?

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.880
Yeah, the way an ant breathes.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.000
But that's facts. It either breathes this way or that way.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.680
This is speculation.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.080
Is it a speculation? If it were just a statement

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.300
this thesis not tested, we wouldn’t do anything with it.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.640
[Printing Press]

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.320
Journals say they determine the quality of research

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.100
they publish by submitting it to expert reviewers.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.680
Reviewer one: This paper is rich
and exciting.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.780
I'm just overwhelmed,

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.920
which is a sign of a marvelous paper.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.320
He's an idiot!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.460
They made up data that he wished, or he or she

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:07.480
wished he had but he didn’t.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.640
So he sees, "Wow, these people did a study

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.360
that I wanted to do, and they got the results that

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.820
I thought should be there. This is great."

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.200
The fields we are concerned about

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.880
put social grievances ahead of objective truth.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.340
So as a simple summery

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.500
we call the problem grievance studies.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.140
Because grievance studies journals

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.940
are so filled with jargon

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.640
phrases like these ...

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.660
even nonsense like the dog rape paper can pass muster.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.000
If papers were written in plain English,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.080
people might see that some of these ideas are false,

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.940
or meaningless.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.840
Inferring from lessons relevant to human and

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.180
dog interactions

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.520
to suggest practical applications

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.060
that disrupt masculinities.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.160
Yes.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:49.700
What!?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.480
That's one thing they like these days

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.160
to disrupt masculinities.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.340
I don't like that concept.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.260
That gets you published, that gets you promoted.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.460
Only in those departments that support that.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:04.769
Well, psychology, your department, leans that way, right?

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:08.120
In some departments, in some areas.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.200
Doesn’t this show journals have a problem?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.060
Is there such a bias here that instead of knowledge,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.960
we're just putting political correctness?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.860
In some areas that is the case,

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.100
but again, that's my feeling.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.380
And I wouldn't do anything until I can actually

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.620
document it.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.260
Is a hoax helping document that? No, it doesn't.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.300
I think it kind of does.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.900
I wouldn't have realized how silly

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.880
some of these journals are without this.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.200
I think something sounds silly,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.220
you watch, look carefully and you'll see

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.900
it's not as silly as you thought it was.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.120
The hoaxers say that in fields that

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.000
end in the word 'studies'

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.340
A culture has developed

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.080
in which only certain conclusions are allowed.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.364
Like those that make whiteness and masculinity

00:04:53.364 --> 00:04:54.420
problematic.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.540
In some places that is correct.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.160
Is that a problem?

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.840
How big of a problem is it?

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.620
Is it worse than hunger?

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:06.940
Is it worse than people shooting each other?

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.280
Why do we need your journal?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.080
Very good point.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:09.900
Sexuality and culture.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.500
Yes. Yes. You know, let's question our assumptions

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.080
because maybe we're making
assumptions

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.420
that we shouldn't be making

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.100
When homosexuality was considered a mental illness.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.420
People pushed and this,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.140
and the psychiatrists got together and said

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.300
It's a perfectly fine thing to choose

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.880
and not to call it mental illness.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.020
So that's the type of thing that, you know, a journal like

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.140
sexuality and culture does is

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.380
discuss.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.540
[Bells]

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.800
Discussion is good, but in journals today,

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.660
only some discussion is allowed.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.780
Some feminists assert, the dildo was an oppressive tool

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.360
of the patriarchy.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.960
This just sounds political.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.540
Political jargon. Yes.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:53.120
But in itself just a sentence, right?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.520
It's just describing some women think that

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.040
using the dildo is a man idea.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.260
But that is a correct statement.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.780
But is it suggests -- a bias.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.300
REFINETTI: Oh, in the wording.
STOSSEL: It's not science, it's just political jargon.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.320
Correct correct.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.360
There is some jargon that is used.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.260
I don't like much.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.800
And in certain areas you just learn to live with it.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.860
In your field, the jargon just goes one way,

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.200
men are the problem.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.180
Yes. And actually I do have a problem with that.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:24.980
You publish it.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.220
It doesn't mean I agree with what they found out.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.420
Shouldn't there be a little more diversity in your field?

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.880
That's a general thing that we hear

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.660
in university campuses, right?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.260
That most people are on the left.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:40.700
A National Association of Scholars report

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.620
found that in liberal arts colleges

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:45.920
democrats outnumber republicans 10:1

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.260
I think it's very reasonable -- because what happens?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:51.140
What is the job of learning?

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:56.320
Is questioning assumptions that are not traditional.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.500
So not being traditional, not being conservative,

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.280
is part of the job of learning.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.840
Being more open to new ideas,

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:09.240
which is, you know, what being a liberal is.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.940
But this is your left leaning definition.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.140
It's conservatives that proposed changes like

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:16.700
school vouchers,

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.280
privatizing air traffic control,

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.920
all kinds of new programs

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.480
while liberals want more of the same.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.400
Oh, that's an interesting point.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.360
Then the hypothesis is shut down.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.380
See, that's how things work.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.660
You show the idea, you discuss the idea and get it.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.940
Any right leaning article is rejected.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.420
No no, and I think that's the major -

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:44.720
Can you point to a couple in your journal?

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.040
That are right leaning?

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:47.680
Well. Ah.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.540
I wouldn't say right leaning because

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:53.280
we don't like either the extreme left or extreme right.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.580
He has published papers that challenge

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.760
feminist orthodoxy, like this one

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.540
saying the “me too” movement may go too far.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.980
There's a push for the women's side these days,

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.080
which very understandably in a reaction because

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.220
for many for a long time

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.140
there was a push on the men's side.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.460
A researcher who had another opinion

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.620
wouldn't get hired or published.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.360
Correct. If you don't match what most people believe,

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.300
you're considered wrong.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:25.100
But isn't that how humans handle knowledge?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.580
No, say the hoaxers, to learn all sides should be heard.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.600
If they wanted to make their point that

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.500
there are people who are in the extreme left,

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.200
yes, there are people in the extreme left,

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.860
but a hoax in a publication in a journal

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.220
is not going to solve the problem.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.780
It's like, robbing a bank

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:42.580
because you have to feed your children.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.660
It's fine, but it's not fine.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.460
The bank gets robbed,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.460
they update their security systems.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.900
What have you done?

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.680
I don't think at this point we have a real good solution.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.160
I don’t think they do.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.720
I’m grateful that Refinetti was

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.820
willing to have a conversation.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:04.440
But I cheer the hoaxers for revealing that

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.160
much of what passes for scholarship at colleges today

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.180
is bunk.

